Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(storage): atomically claim custom paste names

Context:
Concurrent custom-name POST requests can both pass the eventually consistent Workers KV availability check and silently overwrite one another.

Expected behavior:
A direct custom-name create stores its authoritative body with a conditional R2 write. Concurrent requests for the same available name yield one success and stable 409 conflicts. Expired R2-backed names are reclaimed only with an ETag precondition.

Acceptance criteria:
- deterministic same-name race returns one 200 and one 409
- winning content remains retrievable and reports R2 storage
- concurrent expired-name reclaim has exactly one winner
- existing sequential conflicts and expired-name reuse remain compatible

Constraints:
- generic upstream behavior only; no Feishu concepts
- preserve legacy KV-backed named-paste checks
- no Durable Object, new binding, lock framework, or MPU protocol redesign
- do not modify upstream-sync

Validation:
- RED: Node 22 pnpm exec vitest run worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts -> observed [200, 200]
- GREEN: Node 22 focused suite -> 3 files, 21 tests passed
- REGRESSION: Node 22 full suite -> 22 files, 158 tests passed
- pnpm lint; prettier --check .; pnpm typecheck; pnpm build:frontend; pnpm build; git diff --check -> PASS

